  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pamoja kwa amani/Together for peace project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the ACEAC bishops&apos; general assembly held in Goma in January 2024, convened under the Peace in the Great Lakes initiative, multiple resolutions were passed to enhance unity and cooperation among the bishops as they strive to work together for peace. The bishops pledged to bolster their involvement in subregional peace efforts and to carry out strategic initiatives at both high and local levels, with a specific emphasis on promoting cross-border unity among the communities of border dioceses. This project therefore aims to support the bishops achieve the following: 
1. Hold high level extraordinary dialogue meetings on peace with the presidents of the three countries in the region. 
2. Strengthen cross-boarder cohesion by engaging women and youth to champion peace . 
3. Undertake research to generate evidence on governance and peace issues that the bishops could utilise in their advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
